Framework: **MSTest 4.1 / .NET 10** — class tagged `[TestCategory("Integration")]`
Integration calibration: applied (Mystery Guest, Eager Test, Sleepy Test downgraded per catalog rules).

---

## 🔴 High-Severity Findings

### 1. Conditional Test Logic — `GetUser_ReturnsCorrectType` (line 94)

**Catalog name:** Conditional Test Logic  
**Severity:** **High** — control flow in a test means some assertion paths may never execute.

```csharp
// Lines 101-108 — if/else changes WHICH assertion runs
if (loaded is PremiumUser premium)
{
    Assert.IsTrue(premium.DiscountRate > 0);   // path A
}
else
{
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded!.Name);      // path B
}
```

The test always passes, but you never know **which branch** ran. If `PremiumUser` is never returned by the in-memory repo, the discount-rate check is dead code — a hidden testing gap.

**Fix — split into two deterministic tests:**
```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_WhenStandard_ReturnsCorrectName()
{
    var user = new User("eve@example.com", "Eve");
    _repository.Insert(user);
    var loaded = _repository.GetByEmail("eve@example.com");
    Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded.Name);
}

[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_WhenPremium_HasPositiveDiscount()
{
    var user = new PremiumUser("eve@example.com", "Eve", discountRate: 0.1m);
    _repository.Insert(user);
    var loaded = _repository.GetByEmail("eve@example.com") as PremiumUser;
    Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
    Assert.IsTrue(loaded.DiscountRate > 0);
}
```

**Risk if unfixed:** One branch may be permanently untested, giving false confidence.

---

### 2. Assertion-Free Test (Unknown Test) — `BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors` (line 113)

**Catalog name:** Unknown Test / Empty Test  
**Severity:** **High** — the test passes as long as no exception is thrown, even if data is silently lost.

```csharp
// Lines 113-119 — 100 inserts, zero assertions
[TestMethod]
public void BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors()
{
    for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
    {
        _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));
    }
    // ← nothing verified
}
```

> The method name implies a "does not throw" intent — acknowledged. But if `Insert` silently swallows errors or inserts zero rows, this test still passes.

**Fix — add a count assertion:**
```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void BulkInsert_PersistsAllRecords()
{
    for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
    {
        _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));
    }

    var users = _repository.ListAll();
    Assert.AreEqual(100, users.Count);
}
```

**Risk if unfixed:** False confidence — coverage metrics look great but nothing is verified.

---

## 🟡 Medium-Severity Findings

### 3. Sleepy Test — `NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay` (line 82)

**Catalog name:** Sleepy Test  
**Severity:** **Medium** (downgraded from High — integration-test calibration applied, `[TestCategory("Integration")]`). Still a smell even in integration context because the 3-second sleep makes the suite slower and is inherently non-deterministic.

```csharp
// Line 87 — hard-coded 3-second sleep
Thread.Sleep(3000);
```

**Fix — poll with a timeout instead of sleeping a fixed duration:**
```csharp
[TestMethod]
public async Task NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay()
{
    var user = new User("dave@example.com", "Dave");
    _repository.Insert(user);

    // Poll up to 5 s, checking every 100 ms
    var deadline = DateTime.UtcNow.AddSeconds(5);
    while (DateTime.UtcNow < deadline)
    {
        if (_repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id))
            break;
        await Task.Delay(100);
    }

    Assert.IsTrue(_repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id),
        "Notification was not sent within the timeout window.");
}
```

**Risk if unfixed:** 3 s of wasted wall-clock time per run; flaky failures on slow CI agents if the event takes longer.

---

### 4. Assertion Roulette — `InsertUser_PersistsToDatabase` (line 28)

**Catalog name:** Assertion Roulette  
**Severity:** **Medium** — 4 assertions with no descriptive messages. When one fails, the MSTest output shows the assertion type and values but not *which property* was wrong without reading the code.

```csharp
// Lines 35-38 — four bare assertions, no messages
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name);
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email);
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0);
```

**Fix — add message parameters:**
```csharp
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded, "User should be retrievable after insert");
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name, "Name should round-trip");
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email, "Email should round-trip");
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0, "Auto-generated Id should be positive");
```

**Risk if unfixed:** Slower triage — developers must open the source to understand CI failures.

---

## ✅ Smell-Free Patterns (Well-Designed Tests)

The remaining **4 tests** are clean and well-structured:

| Test | Notes |
|------|-------|
| `UpdateUser_ModifiesExistingRecord` | Clear arrange-act-assert, 2 focused assertions |
| `DeleteUser_RemovesFromDatabase` | Single assertion on absence — crisp |
| `ListUsers_ReturnsAllInserted` | `Assert.AreEqual(3, …)` after inserting 3 items — self-documenting, not a Magic Number |
| `InsertUser_ConcurrentInserts_MaintainsIntegrity` | Proper async/await, count assertion matches setup — good concurrency test |

**Not flagged (calibration applied):**
- **Mystery Guest**: `SqliteConnection("Data Source=:memory:")` is a hermetic in-memory database, not an external resource. ✔️
- **Eager Test**: No test calls 4+ distinct production methods; multi-method calls are appropriate for integration scope. ✔️
- **General Fixture**: Both `_connection` and `_repository` are used by all 8 tests. ✔️
- **Magic Numbers**: `3`, `10`, `100` in assertions all match items added immediately above — contextually obvious. ✔️

---

## 🗓 Prioritized Remediation Plan

| Priority | Smell | Fix | Impact | Effort |
|----------|-------|-----|--------|--------|
| 1 | **Assertion-Free Test** | Add count assertion to `BulkInsert` | Eliminates false-pass risk | ~2 min |
| 2 | **Conditional Test Logic** | Split `GetUser_ReturnsCorrectType` into two tests | Ensures both paths are tested | ~5 min |
| 3 | **Sleepy Test** | Replace `Thread.Sleep(3000)` with poll-and-timeout | Faster suite, less flakiness | ~10 min |
| 4 | **Assertion Roulette** | Add message strings to `InsertUser_PersistsToDatabase` | Faster CI triage | ~2 min |

**Total estimated effort: under 20 minutes.** Priorities 1–2 prevent silent false-passes; 3 reduces flakiness; 4 is a quality-of-life improvement.
